# Enterprise‑Grade Agent Runtime on Supabase — Complete Security & Architecture

## 🛡️ Core Security Principles
- **Zero Trust** — verify every request
- **RLS everywhere** — enable Row Level Security on all exposed tables
- **Service‑role isolation** — keep `service_role` **only** on your backend; never send it to the browser
- **Deny‑by‑default** — explicit allow rules only; anything unspecified = blocked
- **Capability‑based RBAC** — fine‑grained permissions (`github.push`, not just `execute`)
- **Immutable audit logs** — append‑only, no updates/deletes
- **Permission versioning** — track and roll out permission sets
- **Dedicated schema** — `agent_runtime` separates control plane from business data
- **JWKS‑verified JWTs** — no disabled signature checks

---

## 🏗️ Recommended Architecture

```
Frontend (React/Next.js)
  ↓ Uses only ANON key + JWT
Supabase Auth (MFA + PKCE)
